abstract: >
  The Dimensional Substrate Regime Scanning Protocol (dsrsp/0.1) defines a minimal,
  substrate‑agnostic wire format for adding regime awareness to any sensor stack.
  It integrates directly with the Resonance Substrate Model (RSM) and Validation‑Space‑Time
  (vST) engines, enabling modern instruments—ROVs, drones, planetary probes, and
  hypothetical starship scanners—to classify structural, sensory, and environmental
  regimes using a unified grammar. The protocol includes optional intelligent‑life
  probability (ILP) analysis and provides a clean alignment layer for RSM and vST
  engines of varying complexity.
keywords:
